    {
      "short": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\">\n          <li><b>Sharding</b> splits data and writes across machines.</li>\n          <li>The <b>shard key</b> decides where rows live — it must spread load evenly.</li>\n          <li><b>Ranges</b> make hot spots; <b>hashes</b> spread load but scatter range queries.</li>\n          <li>A single <b>hot key</b> needs caching or splitting.</li>\n          <li>Queries off the shard key hit <b>every shard</b>; resharding with % N moves most data.</li>\n        </ul>"
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "next",
        "text": "Next up: <b>Consistent Hashing</b> — add or remove a shard and move only a fraction of the keys."
